And I realize that Jordan is very upset.

1336
01:19:15,179 --> 01:19:18,323
But if I could talk to her, make her see that I'm going to stick by her through this.

1337
01:19:19,344 --> 01:19:21,186
I hope you're not suggesting that you'll marry her.

1338
01:19:26,182 --> 01:19:28,363
I'm not sure what we're going to do.

1339
01:19:28,423 --> 01:19:29,643
We've got a lot to talk about.

1340
01:19:29,683 --> 01:19:30,423
The hell you do.

1341
01:19:31,603 --> 01:19:32,583
The hell you do.

1342
01:19:34,104 --> 01:19:34,744
All right, look.

1343
01:19:35,764 --> 01:19:39,745
I know Jordan a lot better than you do, and I've never seen her as unhappy as she is at this moment.

1344
01:19:40,405 --> 01:19:42,866
She is just not very wise in the ways of the world.

1345
01:19:43,686 --> 01:19:46,487
And right now, what she needs around her are people she can trust.

1346
01:19:47,487 --> 01:19:48,667
She can trust me.

1347
01:19:49,047 --> 01:19:50,047
She doesn't want to see you.

1348
01:19:51,488 --> 01:19:52,808
She doesn't want to even talk to you.

1349
01:19:55,032 --> 01:19:57,033
Just wait here for one moment for me, will you please?

1350
01:20:07,960 --> 01:20:08,900
Good afternoon, Miss Mooney.

1351
01:20:09,121 --> 01:20:09,381
Hi.

1352
01:20:15,344 --> 01:20:17,526
Mr. Mooney, I think I'm just going to... Mr. Flanagan, here.

1353
01:20:19,527 --> 01:20:20,327
What the hell is this?

1354
01:20:20,468 --> 01:20:20,908
That's for you.

1355
01:20:26,185 --> 01:20:27,006
$10,000.

1356
01:20:29,908 --> 01:20:30,909
Is that all your daughter's worth?

1357
01:20:32,210 --> 01:20:34,051
OK. How much will it take?

1358
01:20:34,752 --> 01:20:35,853
I don't want your goddamn money.

1359
01:20:37,334 --> 01:20:39,656
You can't buy me out of Jordan's life.

1360
01:20:40,056 --> 01:20:43,419
You think I'm letting some bartender walk into my family and destroy my daughter's life?

1361
01:20:43,519 --> 01:20:44,239
That is her choice.

1362
01:20:44,279 --> 01:20:44,880
What the hell you say?

1363
01:20:44,900 --> 01:20:45,440
Her choice!

1364
01:20:45,480 --> 01:20:46,201
What the hell you say?

1365
01:20:46,221 --> 01:20:47,202
What is going on here?

1366
01:20:48,203 --> 01:20:50,004
Jordan, I came by here to talk to you.

1367
01:20:50,024 --> 01:20:53,187
Look, if you don't get out of here, Flanagan, I'm going to have you thrown out on the grass.

1368
01:20:55,090 --> 01:20:57,852
Jordan, I know the other night I didn't say the right things.

1369
01:20:57,912 --> 01:20:59,734
God knows I have not done the right things.

1370
01:21:01,135 --> 01:21:03,496
But I think there's a chance for us.

1371
01:21:04,657 --> 01:21:06,018
Brian, there is no us.

1372
01:21:06,299 --> 01:21:08,840
There are just too many things about us that don't work.

1373
01:21:08,961 --> 01:21:09,721
What about the baby?

1374
01:21:10,922 --> 01:21:12,984
I mean, a kid, our kid needs a father.

1375
01:21:15,205 --> 01:21:16,927
Not one that's not going to be around in a year.

1376
01:21:17,147 --> 01:21:19,388
Yeah, with your lifestyle, what kind of a father are you going to have?

1377
01:21:19,408 --> 01:21:21,510
Dad!

1378
01:21:21,530 --> 01:21:23,932
Jordan, I want a second chance.

1379
01:21:26,237 --> 01:21:27,618
No.

1380
01:21:27,638 --> 01:21:29,680
I deserve a second chance.

1381
01:21:29,780 --> 01:21:30,160
No.

1382
01:21:31,922 --> 01:21:34,323
Brian, how am I ever going to know that you're being honest with me?

1383
01:21:35,164 --> 01:21:37,166
I mean, you can barely be honest with yourself.

1384
01:21:37,406 --> 01:21:37,826
Honest?

1385
01:21:39,027 --> 01:21:39,968
Were you so honest?

1386
01:21:40,889 --> 01:21:42,850
Why didn't you tell me you were the original rich chick?

1387
01:21:43,631 --> 01:21:48,755
Because you're so hung up on money, I was afraid that I'd never know how you really felt about me.

1388
01:21:50,056 --> 01:21:50,416
Me.

1389
01:21:50,436 --> 01:21:52,378
How you'd really feel about me.

1390
01:21:56,602 --> 01:22:02,308
This is your father's idea of how to get me out of your life.

1391
01:22:07,254 --> 01:22:10,698
This is how hung up on money I am.

1392
01:22:12,740 --> 01:22:17,906
And as for the way I feel about you, I guess you'll never know.

1393
01:22:31,153 --> 01:22:34,176
Hey, what about us?

1394
01:22:34,216 --> 01:22:35,137
Come on, let us in.

1395
01:22:35,197 --> 01:22:36,558
Henry, it's cold out here.

1396
01:22:36,818 --> 01:22:40,201
Henry, it never means I was free last night.

1397
01:22:40,301 --> 01:22:42,623
You look more like this couch.

1398
01:22:43,043 --> 01:22:43,964
Henry, I'm Doug's friend.

1399
01:22:44,204 --> 01:22:48,148
Look, Mr. Papa doesn't have any friends on a Saturday night.

1400
01:22:48,188 --> 01:22:50,230
Good evening, Henry.

1401
01:22:50,330 --> 01:22:51,090
Hey, hey.

1402
01:22:51,210 --> 01:22:54,213
Hey, hey, where's Doug Cobb?

1403
01:22:54,253 --> 01:22:55,114
He's over there.

1404
01:22:55,134 --> 01:22:55,955
Over there?

1405
01:22:59,772 --> 01:23:01,253
Hey, you!

1406
01:23:01,313 --> 01:23:02,093
You!

1407
01:23:02,894 --> 01:23:03,354
Doug!

1408
01:23:03,414 --> 01:23:04,294
Holy Doug!

1409
01:23:04,714 --> 01:23:05,635
Flanagan!

1410
01:23:06,335 --> 01:23:07,776
My best friend in the world.

1411
01:23:07,856 --> 01:23:08,676
My only friend.

1412
01:23:09,457 --> 01:23:10,077
Piss off, Henry.

1413
01:23:10,117 --> 01:23:10,637
It's okay.

1414
01:23:10,777 --> 01:23:12,478
It's great to see you, my only friend.

1415
01:23:12,958 --> 01:23:13,419
Sit down.

1416
01:23:13,519 --> 01:23:14,019
Sit down.

1417
01:23:14,319 --> 01:23:14,879
I don't know.

1418
01:23:14,899 --> 01:23:17,080
Looks like you've got a lot of friends here this evening.

1419
01:23:17,220 --> 01:23:18,401
Proctologist dream.

1420
01:23:18,481 --> 01:23:18,761
What?

1421
01:23:18,901 --> 01:23:20,222
Wall-to-wall assholes.

1422
01:23:20,902 --> 01:23:22,263
It's great to see you, Flanagan.

1423
01:23:22,323 --> 01:23:24,844
Yes, because you know I've come to pay off my bet.

1424
01:23:25,024 --> 01:23:25,704
Brian!

1425
01:23:26,465 --> 01:23:26,945
Gary!

1426
01:23:29,739 --> 01:23:31,220
What are you doing here?

1427
01:23:31,980 --> 01:23:33,961
I've come to beg and plead for a job.

1428
01:23:34,621 --> 01:23:43,625
It'd be great to get some talent behind the bar.

1429
01:23:44,385 --> 01:23:53,209
Well, let's go somewhere where we can appreciate this.

1430
01:23:53,870 --> 01:23:55,090
Come on.

1431
01:24:03,798 --> 01:24:04,338
Good time?

1432
01:24:04,358 --> 01:24:04,939
Get in there.

1433
01:24:04,999 --> 01:24:06,079
What are you doing out here?

1434
01:24:06,099 --> 01:24:07,320
Get in there and spend some money.

1435
01:24:07,340 --> 01:24:09,381
Keep me in the manner that I'm accustomed to.

1436
01:24:09,401 --> 01:24:10,042
Very good.

1437
01:24:10,082 --> 01:24:10,542
How are you?

1438
01:24:10,562 --> 01:24:12,343
Get in there and spend some money, you two.

1439
01:24:13,323 --> 01:24:15,144
What do you think of my rowing boat?

1440
01:24:16,905 --> 01:24:18,366
Jesus Christ!

1441
01:24:19,047 --> 01:24:20,087
Come aboard, you land lover.

1442
01:24:24,930 --> 01:24:25,910
Buckle of crystal.

1443
01:24:27,751 --> 01:24:29,593
Louis XIII, et voila.

1444
01:24:31,193 --> 01:24:32,074
Shall we let it breathe?

1445
01:24:33,331 --> 01:24:35,833
It hasn't breathed in 50 years.

1446
01:24:35,913 --> 01:24:36,693
It's dead.

1447
01:24:36,913 --> 01:24:38,274
Let's just drink it.

1448
01:24:50,983 --> 01:24:51,763
Health and friendship?

1449
01:24:53,124 --> 01:24:54,205
Life and love.

1450
01:25:03,622 --> 01:25:09,024
Douglas Coughlin, your ship has certainly come in.

1451
01:25:12,485 --> 01:25:13,145
My ship.

1452
01:25:15,065 --> 01:25:18,666
My ship is going down, and I'm going down with it.

1453
01:25:19,367 --> 01:25:19,947
How's that?

1454
01:25:20,547 --> 01:25:21,647
Oh, this is an illusion.

1455
01:25:21,667 --> 01:25:23,908
I'm on my ass.

1456
01:25:23,928 --> 01:25:25,669
I haven't got a pot to piss in.

1457
01:25:26,109 --> 01:25:26,489
Hmm.

1458
01:25:28,189 --> 01:25:29,330
A hundred grand a week.

1459
01:25:29,850 --> 01:25:30,330
Painful.

1460
01:25:31,752 --> 01:25:34,613
I should have read some of your sacred books, young Flanagan.

1461
01:25:36,534 --> 01:25:40,995
The only thing I know about saloons is how to pour whiskey and run my mouth off.

1462
01:25:41,716 --> 01:25:55,180
I knew nothing about insurance... or sales tax or the building code or labor costs or the power company or purchasing or linens.

1463
01:25:55,600 --> 01:25:57,901
Everyone with a hand stuck it in my pocket.

1464
01:25:58,161 --> 01:25:59,542
You must make enough to cover that.

1465
01:26:00,395 --> 01:26:04,096
if I'd stuck to what I know best, which is almost nothing.

1466
01:26:06,057 --> 01:26:12,680
Instead, I put all the cash into commodities and blew the fucking lot.

1467
01:26:14,520 --> 01:26:20,083
On the margin, buy, cover, buy, cover.

1468
01:26:20,103 --> 01:26:21,503
I wanted it fast.

1469
01:26:25,765 --> 01:26:27,045
See the headlines.

1470
01:26:27,826 --> 01:26:28,986
Douglas Coughlin.

1471
01:26:30,355 --> 01:26:32,296
from bartender to billionaire.

1472
01:26:33,456 --> 01:26:39,839
Hey, Doug, take it easy, huh?

1473
01:26:40,579 --> 01:26:41,199
Relax.

1474
01:26:42,620 --> 01:26:48,342
The luck is gone, the brain is shot, but the liquor we still got.

1475
01:26:58,293 --> 01:26:59,654
She knows nothing about this.

1476
01:27:00,674 --> 01:27:02,915
She thinks I'm a fucking hero.

1477
01:27:09,237 --> 01:27:10,357
My princess.

1478
01:27:11,718 --> 01:27:12,538
My dream.

1479
01:27:14,019 --> 01:27:14,939
Oh, baby.

1480
01:27:15,259 --> 01:27:15,939
Not again.

1481
01:27:15,959 --> 01:27:17,900
I want to go home.

1482
01:27:19,100 --> 01:27:19,701
Come here.

1483
01:27:21,461 --> 01:27:26,003
A toast, Flanagan, to the first and last person

1484
01:27:31,430 --> 01:27:31,731
Doug?

1485
01:27:34,120 --> 01:27:34,501
Doug.

1486
01:27:35,163 --> 01:27:35,926
Doug, wake up.

1487
01:27:36,267 --> 01:27:37,171
I want to go home.

1488
01:28:00,258 --> 01:28:02,800
You know you're the only person in the world Doug respects.

1489
01:28:06,524 --> 01:28:07,425
We were a good team once.

1490
01:28:10,468 --> 01:28:11,428
Walk me to my apartment.

1491
01:28:12,489 --> 01:28:13,971
I hate going to that place alone.

1492
01:28:18,895 --> 01:28:19,896
I better check on Doug.

1493
01:28:20,417 --> 01:28:20,737
Please.

1494
01:28:22,759 --> 01:28:25,802
I want to talk about Doug, about his problems.

1495
01:29:04,343 --> 01:29:08,805
Doug says you're incredible with women, a real lady killer.

1496
01:29:10,245 --> 01:29:11,026
Is that what he says?

1497
01:29:13,326 --> 01:29:14,347
What's your secret weapon?

1498
01:29:16,688 --> 01:29:19,709
Well, what you see is what you get.

1499
01:29:39,965 --> 01:29:40,745
What did you do that for?

1500
01:29:40,765 --> 01:29:49,649
I can't make it with my best friend's old lady.

1501
01:29:52,069 --> 01:29:58,131
Am I supposed to live with the same man day in and day out forever and have no one else in my life?

1502
01:29:58,732 --> 01:29:58,992
Yes.

1503
01:29:59,492 --> 01:30:00,292
It's called marriage.

1504
01:30:01,253 --> 01:30:02,613
You wanted this as much as I did.

1505
01:30:03,393 --> 01:30:04,234
That's why you're up here.

1506
01:30:05,134 --> 01:30:06,614
But you can't do it now, can you?

1507
01:30:07,775 --> 01:30:08,395
You're scared.

1508
01:30:11,658 --> 01:30:13,359
I don't know what the fuck I'm doing.

1509
01:30:13,920 --> 01:30:25,829
You're just scared.

1510
01:30:40,060 --> 01:30:40,480
Hey, Doug.

1511
01:30:53,833 --> 01:30:54,473
Help me!

1512
01:30:54,613 --> 01:30:59,575
Somebody help me!

1513
01:30:59,735 --> 01:31:02,296
Somebody help me!

1514
01:31:05,738 --> 01:31:16,323
Is there anything at all you can tell me about what happened tonight?

1515
01:31:34,158 --> 01:31:55,488
The Lord is my shepherd, and he shall not harm me.

1516
01:32:36,456 --> 01:32:40,980
My dearest Brian, a guy like me looks in the mirror.

1517
01:32:41,760 --> 01:32:43,922
He either grins or he starts to fade away.

1518
01:32:45,443 --> 01:32:48,125
And I haven't seen anything to grin about in a long time.

1519
01:32:50,366 --> 01:32:55,030
This may not be the most graceful exit, but I know when the bottle's empty.

1520
01:32:56,211 --> 01:33:00,854
About the only thing I'm really gonna miss is the conversations we had going.

1521
01:33:03,158 --> 01:33:06,241
At least I get the last word, even if I had to mail it in.

1522
01:33:08,904 --> 01:33:09,745
Coughlin's law.

1523
01:33:10,746 --> 01:33:12,988
Bury the dead, they stink up the joint.

1524
01:33:13,008 --> 01:33:16,152
As for the rest of Coughlin's laws, ignore them.

1525
01:33:17,233 --> 01:33:18,935
The guy was always full of shit.

1526
01:33:23,119 --> 01:33:24,961
But I guess you knew that already.

1527
01:33:35,735 --> 01:33:52,962
I know who you are, pal.

1528
01:33:52,982 --> 01:33:55,462
I've been instructed not to let you into the building.

1529
01:33:55,522 --> 01:33:56,783
If you just leave now.

1530
01:33:58,103 --> 01:34:00,825
Look, I just want to talk to her for a few minutes.

1531
01:34:00,865 --> 01:34:01,946
I don't want to cause any trouble.

1532
01:34:02,367 --> 01:34:03,708
Just send her a letter.

1533
01:34:03,868 --> 01:34:04,689
Get your hands off her.

1534
01:34:23,873 --> 01:34:24,433
Where's Jordan?

1535
01:34:24,453 --> 01:34:24,914
She's in there.

1536
01:34:24,994 --> 01:34:25,414
In there?

1537
01:34:25,454 --> 01:34:25,634
Yeah.

1538
01:34:25,714 --> 01:34:27,155
I mean, you can't go in there.

1539
01:34:27,215 --> 01:34:28,436
Open the door.

1540
01:34:28,616 --> 01:34:28,976
Jordan?

1541
01:34:29,016 --> 01:34:29,756
Open the door.

1542
01:34:29,776 --> 01:34:30,116
Jordan.

1543
01:34:31,097 --> 01:34:31,437
Jordan.

1544
01:34:32,017 --> 01:34:32,238
What?

1545
01:34:32,458 --> 01:34:33,478
Jordan, I have to talk to you.

1546
01:34:33,538 --> 01:34:34,339
What's going on?

1547
01:34:34,359 --> 01:34:36,420
Please, there's so many things, I don't know where to begin.

1548
01:34:37,680 --> 01:34:38,281
Doug is dead.

1549
01:34:39,722 --> 01:34:39,982
What?

1550
01:34:40,642 --> 01:34:41,362
He killed himself.

1551
01:34:41,382 --> 01:34:43,444
Oh, Brian.

1552
01:34:43,784 --> 01:34:46,585
He was my best friend, but he was too proud to let me help him.

1553
01:34:46,625 --> 01:34:49,787
He was too proud to show how he felt until it was too late.

1554
01:34:49,867 --> 01:34:51,528
I don't want to make that same mistake, Jordan.

1555
01:34:54,115 --> 01:34:55,636
He pushed right past me into the sitting room.

1556
01:34:55,716 --> 01:34:57,957
I thought I told you to keep that punk out of this house.

1557
01:34:58,217 --> 01:34:58,457
Sorry.

1558
01:34:58,477 --> 01:34:59,158
He kept behind me.

1559
01:34:59,218 --> 01:34:59,438
Jordan?

1560
01:34:59,498 --> 01:35:00,438
Jordan, are you in there?

1561
01:35:00,919 --> 01:35:02,319
I have saved money.

1562
01:35:02,679 --> 01:35:04,500
I've worked out a loan with my uncle for some more.

1563
01:35:04,520 --> 01:35:06,922
With hard work, I know I can turn it into something great.

1564
01:35:06,942 --> 01:35:08,903
Brian, I know you can't.

1565
01:35:08,923 --> 01:35:09,643
I know you can't.

1566
01:35:09,663 --> 01:35:11,464
But really, it doesn't really matter.

1567
01:35:11,484 --> 01:35:11,644
Listen.

1568
01:35:11,704 --> 01:35:12,244
Listen to me.

1569
01:35:12,304 --> 01:35:12,825
Listen to me.

1570
01:35:12,905 --> 01:35:14,005
He was on the elevator before.

1571
01:35:14,025 --> 01:35:14,586
Give me that key.

1572
01:35:15,746 --> 01:35:16,326
I love you.

1573
01:35:16,447 --> 01:35:17,227
I want to marry you.

1574
01:35:17,947 --> 01:35:19,928
I've loved you from the first moment I saw you, Jordan.

1575
01:35:20,809 --> 01:35:21,089
Please.

1576
01:35:22,310 --> 01:35:23,110
Please, come with me.

1577
01:35:24,583 --> 01:35:26,964
Flanagan, get the hell out of my house.

1578
01:35:27,384 --> 01:35:28,104
Jordan, wake up.

1579
01:35:28,504 --> 01:35:29,604
Don't you see why he's come back here?

1580
01:35:29,844 --> 01:35:31,345
He's only come back for one reason, for the money.

1581
01:35:31,365 --> 01:35:31,945
That's not true.

1582
01:35:31,965 --> 01:35:32,985
I don't want to think from you.

1583
01:35:33,005 --> 01:35:34,966
You're not going to get anything, not one penny.

1584
01:35:35,066 --> 01:35:35,686
He's a loser.

1585
01:35:35,726 --> 01:35:37,006
I'm not a loser.

1586
01:35:37,026 --> 01:35:38,027
Please, Jordan, come with me.

1587
01:35:38,107 --> 01:35:39,247
Get him out of here, please.

1588
01:35:39,287 --> 01:35:39,767
Stay out of this.

1589
01:35:39,787 --> 01:35:40,907
This has nothing to do with you.

1590
01:35:40,967 --> 01:35:41,327
Please.

1591
01:35:41,548 --> 01:35:42,608
Throw this bum out of here.

1592
01:35:42,628 --> 01:35:43,268
Come on.

1593
01:35:43,568 --> 01:35:44,209
Don't regret it.

1594
01:35:44,229 --> 01:35:44,789
Just hold it.

1595
01:35:44,809 --> 01:35:45,450
Just hold it.

1596
01:35:45,510 --> 01:35:45,770
No.

1597
